<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 71,480 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 71,480 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 71,480 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 69,683 tonnes on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			17,120	     9,231</p>
<p>    Import cargo			54,360	    60,452</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight ships are expected to sail and eight to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 36,000	Yasmeen		   due</p>
<p>General cargo	   1,400	Ayubia		    8/5</p>
<p>Jet A-1 fuel	   25,000	Chilham Castle	  due</p>
<p>General cargo	   1,021	Margaretha		9/5</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
